00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:56,880
This specifies what is required to inject the query string to cause prototype pollution.

47
00:04:57,420 --> 00:05:00,380
And that's how you find prototype pollution sources.

48
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:10,640
So, you found client-side prototype pollution.

49
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,200
Now, what should you do?

50
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:19,060
Well, you might want to confirm that the site is actually vulnerable by doing a test yourself.

51
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,460
DomInvader makes this easy.

52
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,200
When a source has been found, simply click on the test button.

