158
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:32,480
When using DomInvader to scan at scale,

159
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:37,080
we quickly realised we needed a way to get vulnerabilities out of DomInvader.

160
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:40,480
The solution we came up with was to use callbacks.

161
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:47,700
A callback allows you to call a custom JavaScript function when a source, sync or message is found.

162
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:53,080
You can use this callback to log the results or whatever you decide to do.

163
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:59,980
Returning true or false in the callback enables you to instruct DomInvader to log the results or not.

164
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:02,780
Here's how to add a callback.

165
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,480
Click the DomInvader icon.

166
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:09,200
And then the general settings cog.

167
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:14,540
Then click the sync callback configuration button.

168
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:20,060
This should then show you a deactivated callback because it's greyed out.

169
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:22,340
Click inside the text box.

170
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:27,480
By default, it logs all the data to the console and returns true.

171
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:30,480
Once you are done, click save.

172
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:32,840
And now the callback is active.

173
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:41,700
So if we visit a test case such as the augmented DOM eval test case.

174
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:47,740
